WEBVTT

00:00:17.560 --> 00:00:25.970
How can I tell you this?

00:00:28.400 --> 00:00:37.170
How can I tell you this?

00:00:39.310 --> 00:00:47.620
I cannot touch you

00:00:50.220 --> 00:00:54.230
But I...

00:00:54.230 --> 00:00:58.490
...can kill you

00:01:01.130 --> 00:01:05.570
I'm so sad to say to you...

00:01:05.570 --> 00:01:10.570
...but don't put your face so close to me

00:01:11.980 --> 00:01:16.020
Now I hear you say my name...

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:25.010
...so I cross the light to be with you

00:01:34.470 --> 00:01:36.200
Hey, Daniel?

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:37.300
Huh?

00:01:37.440 --> 00:01:40.740
There may be no such thing as coincidence.

00:01:40.870 --> 00:01:43.310
What are you talking about, Momo?

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.300
Everyone the main character
meets acts as his guide.

00:01:48.510 --> 00:01:50.070
Like in a Role Playing Game.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:54.690
Really? But I don't really know
what you're trying to say.

00:01:53.120 --> 00:01:58.060
Beyond the Light.

00:01:55.960 --> 00:01:59.580
Would you like to play this game with me?

00:02:10.370 --> 00:02:12.800
FATHER 2,
<i>BRAVES WORD,</i>
COSMO OCEAN,
THE CASE OF THE
MANGA MURDERS
<i>SPACE MONKEY</i>

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:15.710
This isn't your room...

00:02:15.710 --> 00:02:18.280
...so why is there this much
video game software here?

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.080
Granddad liked RPG's.

00:02:29.690 --> 00:02:32.950
Shall we leave it there for a while longer?

00:02:33.430 --> 00:02:34.890
Yeah.

00:02:41.570 --> 00:02:42.300
What?

00:02:42.900 --> 00:02:44.700
<i>From Granddad</i>
<i>to Kantaro</i>

00:02:57.550 --> 00:02:59.040
Kantaro?

00:03:02.020 --> 00:03:03.390
I found this.

00:03:07.660 --> 00:03:17.000
TO MY GOOD COMRADE KANTARO.
\h\hI THINK I'VE REMINISCED ABOUT THE PAST QUITE ENOUGH,
\h\h\h\hSO WHAT DO YOU SAY TO ONE LAST GAME TOGETHER?
\h\h\h\h\h\hYOU WILL BE THE HERO OF THE STORY AND SET OUT ON A JOURNEY.
\h\h\h\h\h\h\h\hAND THEN YOU WILL FIND THE TREASURE. WELL, LET US BEGIN.

00:03:08.190 --> 00:03:11.000
"To my good comrade, Kantaro."

00:03:11.000 --> 00:03:14.170
"I think I've reminisced about
the past quite enough...

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:17.000
"...so what do you say to
one last game together?

00:03:17.470 --> 00:03:21.640
"You will become the hero of the story
and head out on a journey."

00:03:21.640 --> 00:03:26.010
"And then, you will find the treasure.
Well, let us begin."

00:03:30.220 --> 00:03:31.810
Kantaro?

00:03:32.750 --> 00:03:34.980
T... Tomato.

00:03:39.330 --> 00:03:40.690
What is it?

00:03:40.690 --> 00:03:42.960
What do you mean, what is it?

00:03:42.960 --> 00:03:47.570
You just told the teacher that
you were sitting out of study camp.

00:03:47.570 --> 00:03:50.360
What's it to you? I have things to do at home.

00:03:52.870 --> 00:03:56.400
That reminds me. I ran into your mom yesterday.

00:03:58.980 --> 00:04:01.810
She asked me to look after you
while you were at study camp.

00:04:01.810 --> 00:04:04.340
She asked me to make sure you stay focused.

00:04:06.450 --> 00:04:08.920
Would you like to explain...

00:04:08.920 --> 00:04:10.260
...Kantaro Ichihara?

00:04:10.260 --> 00:04:13.350
Well, uh, you see...

00:04:14.830 --> 00:04:20.200
...I have to go to my grandfather's home town.

00:04:23.940 --> 00:04:25.240
All by yourself?

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:27.070
Yeah.

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:28.740
In secret from your mom?

00:04:28.740 --> 00:04:30.110
I have to!

00:04:30.810 --> 00:04:33.010
This is a game between me and my grandfather!

00:04:34.380 --> 00:04:35.310
NANAKUSA STATION
(NORTH ENTRANCE)

00:04:35.310 --> 00:04:39.150
TSUGARU
LIQUOR
STORE

00:04:36.950 --> 00:04:39.150
I never imagined you would
actually skip out on study camp...

00:04:39.150 --> 00:04:41.950
...to play that game you were talking about.

00:04:41.950 --> 00:04:43.560
Are you stupid?

00:04:43.560 --> 00:04:45.650
You do realize what kind of pressure
we're under right now, don't you?

00:04:46.260 --> 00:04:49.500
We're in our 3rd year of middle school,
fighting for entrance to high school!

00:04:49.500 --> 00:04:52.430
E-even I know that!

00:04:52.730 --> 00:04:53.930
Don't make fun of me.

00:04:53.930 --> 00:04:56.230
Then what are you doing here?

00:04:56.970 --> 00:05:00.370
We depart for study camp
from the school, today!

00:05:01.570 --> 00:05:02.970
You really are stupid.

00:05:03.280 --> 00:05:05.040
Well, you see...

00:05:05.040 --> 00:05:06.530
Kanta!

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:10.710
You are going to the school, aren't you?

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:12.440
U-uh...

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:16.450
I'm sorry, Tomato. I can't go to school!

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:21.150
I just have to see this thing
with granddad through!

00:05:23.200 --> 00:05:24.560
Kanta...

00:05:24.560 --> 00:05:25.970
Yes?

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.800
Your last exams were all over the place.

00:05:28.800 --> 00:05:31.000
Do you really think you can leave it like this?

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:33.430
N-no, I don't.

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:35.700
Then why?

00:05:36.710 --> 00:05:38.300
I made a decision.

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:42.550
Very well...

00:05:47.790 --> 00:05:49.450
I'm coming with you.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:51.780
What?!

00:05:55.130 --> 00:05:56.960
Granddad, there! Attack it now!

00:05:58.300 --> 00:05:59.800
You... Take that!

00:05:59.800 --> 00:06:01.270
Right on!

00:06:01.270 --> 00:06:03.860
Whew, I finally beat him.

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:08.610
That attack tomato was so tough.

00:06:08.610 --> 00:06:12.080
You need more practice if you're having trouble
beating small fry like that, Granddad.

00:06:12.080 --> 00:06:14.050
That reminds me...

00:06:14.050 --> 00:06:16.750
...how has our girl Tomato
been keeping recently?

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:21.690
Tomato? She became the class leader,
and is now the president of the student council.

00:06:21.690 --> 00:06:24.160
Really? When she was a child...

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:27.890
...she was such a quiet girl,
and her face would turn as red as her name.

00:06:28.490 --> 00:06:32.100
Now she's blazing down the path of
King of Student Councils.

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:35.400
She's a pretty good pairing
with an easygoing lad like you.

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:39.530
Actually, I'm always the target of her attacks.

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:43.940
That's because she worries about you.

00:06:50.180 --> 00:06:51.380
What is it?

00:06:51.380 --> 00:06:53.010
Nothing.

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:56.290
I'm glad it's not raining.

00:06:56.290 --> 00:06:57.480
Yeah.

00:07:00.360 --> 00:07:03.230
Have there been any interesting
TV shows recently?

00:07:03.230 --> 00:07:04.600
Not really.

00:07:04.600 --> 00:07:06.720
Um...

00:07:11.600 --> 00:07:14.870
By the way, why aren't you in uniform?

00:07:14.870 --> 00:07:17.670
What? Uh...

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.250
That's funny.

00:07:21.250 --> 00:07:22.810
Well...

00:07:23.050 --> 00:07:25.080
You know! Don't you remember?

00:07:25.080 --> 00:07:27.950
The teacher said we didn't really
have to wear our uniforms?

00:07:28.950 --> 00:07:30.060
I see.

00:07:30.060 --> 00:07:31.610
Exactly!

00:07:33.960 --> 00:07:35.530
Do I look weird?

00:07:35.530 --> 00:07:37.460
Not at all.

00:07:38.630 --> 00:07:42.760
Actually, it's an improvement.
I was just thinking how fashionable you looked.

00:07:43.900 --> 00:07:45.800
Y-you think so?

00:07:46.040 --> 00:07:47.560
S-sure.

00:07:57.850 --> 00:07:58.650
What the?

00:07:58.650 --> 00:07:59.650
What is it?

00:07:59.650 --> 00:08:01.240
I heard a bell.

00:08:06.190 --> 00:08:07.780
I can't hear anything.

00:08:08.530 --> 00:08:10.190
Maybe I'm imagining things.

00:08:22.310 --> 00:08:24.830
Oh! You need to transfer here, don't you?

00:08:30.680 --> 00:08:32.380
Hey, Granddad?

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:36.690
Why do you like games so much?

00:08:36.690 --> 00:08:40.530
Huh? How can I explain it?

00:08:40.530 --> 00:08:42.150
They're exciting.

00:08:43.530 --> 00:08:45.000
Exciting?

00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:47.430
Because I don't know where I'll go next...

00:08:47.930 --> 00:08:52.060
...who I'll meet, and where I'll end up.

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:55.540
It's something...

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:59.200
...that only someone who plays the game
to the end can understand.

00:09:08.590 --> 00:09:11.520
What is the purpose of a 20 minute stopover?!

00:09:16.500 --> 00:09:17.960
Eat.

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:20.870
It's easy to get irritated when you're hungry.

00:09:20.870 --> 00:09:24.340
Uh, right. Thank you for the food.

00:09:24.340 --> 00:09:25.800
Here's tea.

00:09:36.220 --> 00:09:37.710
Have some deep fried chicken too.

00:09:38.120 --> 00:09:39.080
Sure.

00:09:39.080 --> 00:09:41.590
Tomato, good job.

00:09:41.590 --> 00:09:43.560
Huh?

00:09:48.490 --> 00:09:51.760
Come to think of it, why are you
carrying a lunch with you?

00:09:51.760 --> 00:09:54.470
Don't they feed you in study camp?

00:09:54.470 --> 00:09:57.300
What? Uh, you know...

00:09:57.300 --> 00:10:00.240
...they said that you could bring
a lunch on the first day.

00:10:00.740 --> 00:10:03.310
I am the president of the student council,
so they expect it of me!

00:10:03.310 --> 00:10:06.280
I don't think that has anything to do
with being president.

00:10:06.610 --> 00:10:10.170
I has everything to do with it!
You'd be amazed at what is expected of me!

00:10:15.550 --> 00:10:17.920
Oh, what a nice breeze.

00:10:22.860 --> 00:10:25.190
I can smell the ocean.

00:10:26.270 --> 00:10:27.730
Hey, Kanta!

00:10:27.730 --> 00:10:28.930
Huh?

00:10:28.930 --> 00:10:30.370
Wanna check it out?

00:10:30.370 --> 00:10:32.040
Check out what?

00:10:32.040 --> 00:10:33.630
The ocean.

00:10:46.790 --> 00:10:48.380
We can't stay long!

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:53.690
If we miss this train,
it's 2 hours until the next one.

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:56.200
Aw...

00:10:56.200 --> 00:10:58.460
I guess that's it for summer.

00:11:00.370 --> 00:11:03.960
I didn't go to the beach once this year.

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:06.870
And I bought a swimsuit too.

00:11:08.270 --> 00:11:10.000
I thought it would be last time.

00:11:11.440 --> 00:11:13.970
It would have been nice to go to the beach.

00:11:16.150 --> 00:11:18.480
Was it a risqué swimsuit?

00:11:18.480 --> 00:11:19.950
Perv.

00:11:20.450 --> 00:11:22.440
Look, seagulls!

00:11:26.530 --> 00:11:28.960
It would be nice to fly like a bird.

00:11:30.100 --> 00:11:32.030
We can't fly, so we walk.

00:11:33.070 --> 00:11:38.040
Granddad always said,
"If you don't have wings, just hoof it."

00:11:38.040 --> 00:11:40.660
That sounds like something he might say.

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:45.710
I liked visiting your house in elementary school.

00:11:46.450 --> 00:11:48.950
He taught me how to play with flat marbles.

00:11:48.950 --> 00:11:52.610
But your grandpa would always
play until he won.

00:11:53.120 --> 00:11:54.990
He was the king of the brats.

00:11:54.990 --> 00:11:56.150
Yeah.

00:12:20.110 --> 00:12:21.640
Is something wrong?

00:12:22.550 --> 00:12:24.020
I just saw those kids...

00:12:35.390 --> 00:12:38.030
This is your grandpa's home town?

00:12:38.030 --> 00:12:39.600
Yeah.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:41.590
The sunset sure is pretty.

00:12:42.430 --> 00:12:43.490
Tomato...

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:44.470
What?

00:12:44.600 --> 00:12:48.160
I totally forgot about this,
but what are you gonna do?

00:12:46.340 --> 00:12:47.170
BUS SCHEDULE

00:12:49.740 --> 00:12:52.140
I was planning to sleep
under a tree or something...

00:12:52.540 --> 00:12:56.040
I'll be fine. I have a little money.

00:12:56.180 --> 00:12:58.170
I took it out of the bank yesterday.

00:12:58.850 --> 00:13:00.790
For study camp?

00:13:00.790 --> 00:13:03.380
You need money wherever you go.

00:13:04.390 --> 00:13:06.050
Okay, let's look for a place to stay.

00:13:06.530 --> 00:13:08.550
Wait, does this tiny village
even have a place to stay?

00:13:09.060 --> 00:13:11.360
What? It doesn't?

00:13:11.500 --> 00:13:13.120
Does it look like it has?

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:15.660
INN
"The Spicy Radish"

00:13:16.740 --> 00:13:19.070
Yes. We're brother and sister.

00:13:19.200 --> 00:13:21.770
We were on our way to visit our grandparents...

00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:25.470
GUEST NAME

00:13:21.770 --> 00:13:25.470
...but we missed our connection
and there were no more trains for the day.

00:13:25.710 --> 00:13:27.280
What a shame.

00:13:27.280 --> 00:13:28.750
Thank you for your help.

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:37.080
I'm impressed, President.

00:13:37.490 --> 00:13:40.980
You have to stand strong or
people will doubt you.

00:13:42.360 --> 00:13:44.660
Well, I'm going to have a bath.

00:13:44.660 --> 00:13:45.460
Uh, sure.

00:13:45.600 --> 00:13:47.620
You should do the same.

00:13:47.770 --> 00:13:48.560
Yes, ma'am.

00:13:55.740 --> 00:13:57.940
<i>BATH</i>

00:14:09.520 --> 00:14:10.920
Kanta?

00:14:12.190 --> 00:14:13.820
What are you doing?

00:14:15.790 --> 00:14:17.630
Haven't you had your bath yet?

00:14:17.630 --> 00:14:19.120
Actually...

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:21.390
What's wrong?

00:14:21.570 --> 00:14:23.770
N-nothing.

00:14:23.770 --> 00:14:27.870
We can't eat our supper
until you've had your bath.

00:14:27.870 --> 00:14:29.600
Oh, right.

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.170
Is it too noisy for you?

00:14:37.720 --> 00:14:39.620
No...

00:14:39.620 --> 00:14:42.110
It'll be your turn in a bit.

00:14:46.190 --> 00:14:47.560
What is it?

00:14:47.560 --> 00:14:50.330
I just heard a bell.

00:14:50.330 --> 00:14:53.060
Huh? I didn't hear anything.

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.260
It's the Reaper.

00:14:57.400 --> 00:14:58.160
Huh?

00:14:58.540 --> 00:15:02.870
She's a remarkably pretty little lady...

00:15:03.480 --> 00:15:06.840
...she's very small and white.

00:15:07.610 --> 00:15:09.640
What game are you talking about?

00:15:10.320 --> 00:15:11.910
Nah...

00:15:13.050 --> 00:15:14.540
Kantaro.

00:15:16.220 --> 00:15:20.520
I think my game is about to end.

00:15:32.070 --> 00:15:33.400
Can't sleep?

00:15:35.170 --> 00:15:36.640
Y-yeah.

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:39.040
Me neither.

00:15:39.910 --> 00:15:41.970
I was thinking about Granddad.

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:44.010
Huh?

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:49.350
Just a little before he died,
he said he had seen the Reaper.

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:50.620
Reaper?

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:55.920
And he said that she was
a small, white, cute little girl.

00:15:57.000 --> 00:15:58.930
He probably made it up.

00:15:59.060 --> 00:16:00.760
I wonder.

00:16:00.900 --> 00:16:03.030
It's so easy to trick you.

00:16:03.640 --> 00:16:05.100
What?

00:16:06.200 --> 00:16:08.730
I'm moving.

00:16:09.170 --> 00:16:11.770
What? Are you tricking me now?

00:16:12.840 --> 00:16:14.710
It's the truth.

00:16:15.380 --> 00:16:17.580
I think I'm going somewhere far away.

00:16:18.750 --> 00:16:21.120
I don't think I'll be able to see you again.

00:16:21.250 --> 00:16:22.520
How come?

00:16:22.650 --> 00:16:25.850
It's what my mom and dad want.

00:16:29.330 --> 00:16:33.290
I'm not nearly as tough
as everyone seems to think I am.

00:16:34.130 --> 00:16:38.870
I like to pretend I'm tough.
I tend to do things by myself...

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:41.930
...even though I want help,
but I never ask for help.

00:16:43.010 --> 00:16:46.880
Before I knew it, everyone
started depending on me.

00:16:47.610 --> 00:16:50.080
I kind of enjoyed it.

00:16:50.780 --> 00:16:53.180
I know that. You don't have to tell me...

00:16:53.320 --> 00:16:55.580
...because I already know that.

00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:58.250
I've always known that about you.

00:16:59.090 --> 00:17:03.890
I knew you were pretending
to be tough and independent.

00:17:05.300 --> 00:17:10.530
I never had my act together,
I was just forced into it.

00:17:12.000 --> 00:17:16.580
The truth is, I always want
to lean on someone else...

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.600
...just like a normal person.

00:17:18.980 --> 00:17:23.210
Then do it. You should definitely
lean on someone for a change.

00:17:24.380 --> 00:17:28.610
You can start by leaning on me.

00:17:30.160 --> 00:17:33.790
Okay, maybe I will, for a while.

00:17:33.790 --> 00:17:38.060
S-sure, go for it. But I don't have any money.

00:17:38.060 --> 00:17:40.590
That's okay. For now...

00:17:41.370 --> 00:17:44.170
...would it be okay if I snuggled up in your bed?

00:17:44.170 --> 00:17:45.690
Of course.

00:17:46.810 --> 00:17:49.370
What?! Th-that's a bit too...

00:17:50.040 --> 00:17:51.510
Uh...

00:17:54.150 --> 00:17:55.440
I'm kidding.

00:17:59.890 --> 00:18:01.380
My granddad...

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:05.720
...he said that there was this girl
he really liked when he was a kid.

00:18:06.630 --> 00:18:09.290
She had hair as red as a sunset...

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:12.060
...and they promised to always be friends...

00:18:12.060 --> 00:18:14.330
...but they got split up.

00:18:15.830 --> 00:18:19.530
I think he's buried something
that has his memories of her.

00:18:20.570 --> 00:18:23.670
That's what I came here to find.

00:18:24.380 --> 00:18:28.540
I wasn't going to tell you about it because it's a
private game between Granddad and me...

00:18:30.720 --> 00:18:32.180
You'll find it.

00:18:34.420 --> 00:18:37.050
I know you'll be able to find it.

00:18:38.520 --> 00:18:40.010
Yeah.

00:18:42.660 --> 00:18:43.500
What?!

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:44.930
This is a map?

00:18:45.200 --> 00:18:47.720
You'll never find it using this.

00:18:48.630 --> 00:18:51.240
Did he leave any other hints?

00:18:51.240 --> 00:18:52.240
No.

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:56.410
I have money, but not enough money
for another night at an inn.

00:18:56.410 --> 00:18:58.310
We have to find it today.

00:19:25.240 --> 00:19:27.800
This is hopeless!
I have no idea where it could be.

00:19:29.040 --> 00:19:30.970
Want to take a break?

00:19:31.980 --> 00:19:34.040
This could be game over.

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:46.490
Kanta?

00:19:46.490 --> 00:19:48.980
Could it be? That's impossible.

00:19:58.870 --> 00:20:00.960
Granddad as a little boy?

00:20:47.990 --> 00:20:50.020
Is this...

00:20:50.020 --> 00:20:51.720
...a marble?

00:20:56.430 --> 00:20:57.430
Oh...

00:20:57.430 --> 00:20:58.430
Huh?

00:20:58.430 --> 00:20:59.900
I see it.

00:20:59.900 --> 00:21:01.390
See what?

00:21:01.930 --> 00:21:04.030
I see you and me...

00:21:06.970 --> 00:21:08.440
It's a secret.

00:21:10.210 --> 00:21:11.980
What?

00:21:11.980 --> 00:21:15.750
<i>FOR</i>
<i>KANTARO</i>

00:21:12.610 --> 00:21:13.680
Hey...

00:21:13.780 --> 00:21:15.750
That wasn't there a second ago.

00:21:19.220 --> 00:21:22.220
NOW IT'S YOUR TURN
TO FIND YOUR TREASURE,

00:21:20.990 --> 00:21:24.650
"Now it's your turn to find your treasure."

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:31.260
I'll come and see you.

00:21:31.260 --> 00:21:32.660
What?

00:21:33.600 --> 00:21:37.090
It doesn't matter how far away you are.
I'll come and see you.

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:40.170
Sure.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:47.850
How long do I have to stay like this?

00:21:47.850 --> 00:21:50.470
Oh, yeah. You can change back now, Daniel.

00:21:57.720 --> 00:22:03.320
Wait, why did I have to assume
human form anyway?

00:22:03.760 --> 00:22:07.570
Because you'd startle them if they saw you talk.

00:22:07.570 --> 00:22:13.040
Oh, right. But I never said
anything the whole time.

00:22:13.040 --> 00:22:15.170
What? Really?

00:22:15.710 --> 00:22:20.040
You know, Momo, I think
you were enjoying yourself.

00:22:20.180 --> 00:22:23.510
What? But why wouldn't I? I was playing a game.

00:22:24.720 --> 00:22:26.650
Don't you think?

00:22:49.810 --> 00:22:55.440
Born out of a deep sleep...

00:22:55.980 --> 00:23:03.650
...I wonder why can't I stop crying?

00:23:05.160 --> 00:23:12.890
A gentle breeze blows through my white hair...

00:23:13.730 --> 00:23:20.070
...conveying each and every little word

00:23:21.810 --> 00:23:30.650
Within my arms are so many lives...

00:23:30.650 --> 00:23:38.050
...so fleetingly, so lovingly extinguished

00:23:38.560 --> 00:23:46.900
They dance white and high into the night sky...

00:23:47.370 --> 00:23:55.100
...and I keep watch over them, ever vigilant

00:23:59.980 --> 00:24:04.550
Next Episode

00:24:00.480 --> 00:24:03.180
You cannot stay a child forever...

00:24:03.550 --> 00:24:06.890
...but please, don't be in such
a hurry to grow up.

00:24:06.890 --> 00:24:09.720
Next episode: "Autumn Magic."

00:24:09.920 --> 00:24:14.090
This is the sad and sweet story
of a reaper in white.

00:24:11.990 --> 00:24:14.960
Autumn Magic.
